<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 7.939 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 7.939 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 7.939 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination of three direct sales of government paper and eight repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The direct sales were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>150 million  349 days</p>
<p>150 million  181 days</p>
<p>150 million   90 days</p>
<p>The direct sales were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>	800 million   34 days</p>
<p>	800 million   28 days</p>
<p>	850 million   26 days</p>
<p>	850 million   21 days</p>
<p>	850 million   12 days</p>
<p>	  1.100 bln   11 days</p>
<p>	  1.500 bln    6 days</p>
<p>	739 million    3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
